# {{ app_name }} test harness

Claude drives BA-written test cases against {{ app_name }}: compile the workbook into specs, run each spec through the
CLI, judge the evidence, report to Excel. Three skills carry the procedure; the CLI carries every side effect.

- Run everything as `uv run --env-file .env harness <command>`; `harness --help` lists the commands.
- Never run SQL that changes data and never call the app's API outside the CLI.
- `--yes` executes `run-case` and `revert`. Do not pass it until the user has seen the plan and said go.
- A `PENDING_REVERT` banner means changes are sitting in QA. Fix that first, always.
- No `harness.toml` yet means the harness has not been set up for the app: use the harness-setup skill.
- Skills: `.claude/skills/harness-setup` (point the harness at the app), `.claude/skills/test-compile` (workbook to
  specs), `.claude/skills/test-run` (spec to verdict and report).
- Edit only app-owned files: `harness.toml`, `.env`, `specs/`, `docs/glossary.md`, `docs/schema.md`, `docs/api.md`,
  `docs/outputs.md`. Everything else comes from the template and `copier update` overwrites it.
- Local demo and QA setup: `docs/setup.md`. Checks: `uv run pytest`, `uv run pre-commit run --all-files`.
